    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Four pitch mix but mostly uses a low 90s fastball and low 80s slider. \n The fastball has touched 95 mph at its peak and it plays well up in the zone.\n His slider flashes plus potential, but he doesn't show enough consistency.\n When on it shows hard tilt in the 83 85 mph range and gets bad swings from opposing hitters.\n Also throws a slower curveball with more 12 to 6 shape \n Has a mid 80s changeup with some tumble as well, but doesn't use it much.\n Interesting tools, if he can add some velo he probably could pop a bit as a relief pitcher with the fastball/slider mix.",
